@RokeJulianLockhart that’s probably an issue with the validator as the text is invalid XML. it’s invalid becuase of the unescaped `>` that appears in what _looks_ like the “outer” `<?ignore` closer `?>`.

`xmllint` automatically turns it into `?&gt;` while Safari, Firefox, and Chrome all render the document as `comment ?>`.

_Edit_: Oops, sorry for speaking too quickly. I was thinking of a stray `<` which would _have_ to be escaped at `&lt;`, but then in review of the spec `>` is not mandated to be escaped. After having this pointed out, I see that the linter simply updated an optional escaping, but the gist is the same: we have a text `closer ?>` node there, not a closing processing instruction node.
